-- Dark Chaos - companion pet sizes (2026-11-17, generated by retroport_tools/dc_pet_scale_audit.py).
--
-- Rampage was ten times too big. Retail reuses big boss and creature models for many battle pets and shrinks them
-- on the server: TrinityCore creature_template_model.DisplayScale (Rampage: gorillabossdead at 0.1). Our pet
-- generators copied the two client factors (CreatureModelData.ModelScale, CreatureDisplayInfo.CreatureModelScale)
-- but left DisplayScale at 1. Retail values come from TDB_full_world_1200.26021, matched by species name, else by
-- model + texture + display scale. They are applied only where our .m2 is retail's file: its Stand bounds equal
-- retail's GeoBox.
-- The first batch (3461230-3461277) also still had its old 0.18-0.25 values, because
-- 2026_06_20_00_dc_pet_fixup_scale.sql never reached the DB. Those pets were microscopic.
-- Pets with no retail witness (mostly the Ascension imports) are shrunk only when oversized (longest side > 2 yd).
-- They take the value CoA uses for the same companion when it fits our data, else the 1.2 x 1.8 yd companion box.
-- Only DisplayScale changes; no DBC change. Re-runnable.

